My take being:
  > statically predict target class for an object
  > if that fails use CHA at runtime to prove single class possibility and do a direct call
  > if that fails use inline caching based on first hit

  > only if all of the above fail does it revert back to the megamorphic stub jump
    which does full v-table scan

